{title: Fishin in the Dark}
{artist: Nitty Gritty Dirt Band}
{key: C}
{comment: Chart adapted from chord sheet — verify arrangement}
{comment: Structure: V C V C C}

{start_of_verse}
[C]Lazy yellow moon comin' up tonight, shinin' through the trees
[F]Crickets are singin' and lightning bugs are floatin' on the breeze
Baby get [C]ready
[C]Across the field where the creek turns back by the old stump road
[F]I'm gonna take you to a special place that nobody knows
Baby get [C]ready, oooh [G]oohooh
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]You and me going fishin' in the dark
[C]Lying on our backs and counting the stars
Where the cool [F]grass grows
[C]Down by the river in the full moonlight
[C]We'll be fallin' in love in the middle of the night
Just movin' [F]slow
[Dm]Stayin' the whole night [G]through
[Dm]Feels so good to be with [C]you
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
[C]Spring is almost over and the summer's comin', the days are gettin' long
[F]Waited all winter for the time to be right, just to take you along
Baby get [C]ready
[C]And it don't matter if we sit forever and the fish don't bite
[F]We'll jump in the river and cool ourselves from the heat of the night
Baby get [C]ready, ooh [G]oohooh
{end_of_verse}

